Hi everyone! My friend Jack's company HelmGuard just raised for his AI security startup. Here's the blurb below if people are interested:

&gt; At HelmGuard, we believe that the way institutions build trust is undergoing a fundamental shift. First, critical national infrastructure providers and enterprises will start relying on AI-native firms for core functions. Then, they will adopt agents internally for long-horizon tasks. This will shift trust building away from human-to-human, to human-to-agent and finally to agent-to-agent. Our bet is that HelmGuard will be the rails for human-to-human, human-to-agent and agent-to-agent trust. We're already serving this role at critical national infrastructure providers and other large institutions across Europe, North America and APAC.
&gt; 
&gt; We've just raised $7M from leading UK and US funds, plus executives and board members at Meta and Isomorphic Labs. We're looking for new hires to join our three person team in central London (in-person) with expansion plans to the US later this year. We'll be paying top-10% London base + pre-Series A equity.
&gt; 
&gt; Please see our job board here: <https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/helmguard|jobs.ashbyhq.com/helmguard>

